# Casparel mobile — example environment
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) for local builds, or set these as EAS
# environment variables / secrets for `eas build`.

# ── RevenueCat (public SDK keys — safe to ship in the client bundle) ──────────
# From RevenueCat dashboard → Project → API keys → "Public app-specific" keys.
# The app reads the platform-matching key at runtime (see utils/revenuecat.ts).
# Without them the paywall degrades to "purchases unavailable" rather than
# failing, so a build is still usable — but it cannot sell anything.
EXPO_PUBLIC_RC_IOS_KEY=appl_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
EXPO_PUBLIC_RC_ANDROID_KEY=goog_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Google AdMob + RevenueCat Ads ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# App IDs are consumed by app.config.js at native build time. Development falls
# back to Google's official sample App IDs, but production must set real IDs.
ADMOB_ANDROID_APP_ID=ca-app-pub-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx~xxxxxxxxxx
ADMOB_IOS_APP_ID=ca-app-pub-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx~xxxxxxxxxx

# Native dashboard ad-unit IDs are public identifiers. In development the app
# uses Google's native test unit; release builds render no sponsored card until
# the platform-specific production unit is configured.
EXPO_PUBLIC_ADMOB_ANDROID_DASHBOARD_NATIVE_AD_UNIT_ID=ca-app-pub-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx/xxxxxxxxxx
EXPO_PUBLIC_ADMOB_IOS_DASHBOARD_NATIVE_AD_UNIT_ID=ca-app-pub-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx/xxxxxxxxxx

# RevenueCat Ads is a tracker, not an ad network. Enable Ads beta in RevenueCat
# and impression-level ad revenue (ILRD) in AdMob for revenue events to appear.
# Casparel requests non-personalized ads and education-focused keywords; use
# AdMob content/category controls as the enforcement layer for allowed creatives.

# ── API host ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# An override, not a requirement: utils/api-host.ts defaults to casparel.com,
# so a build that forgets this still talks to production instead of to nothing.
# Every eas.json profile sets it explicitly; set it here to point a local run
# at somewhere else. The scheme and any trailing slash are optional.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_DOMAIN=staging.casparel.com
